<section>
 <h2>Online WebP to PNG Converter: Free, No Watermark</h2>
 <p> Convert WebP images to PNG format instantly with this free online tool. PNG is a lossless image format
 supported by virtually every application, browser, and operating system. If you've downloaded a WebP image
 and need it in PNG for editing, printing, or wider compatibility, this converter provides a fast and
 hassle-free solution: no software installation, no signup, and no watermarks.
 </p>
 <p> For animated WebP files, the server converter automatically produces an APNG (Animated PNG) file, preserving
 all animation frames and timing. APNG maintains the high-quality visuals of WebP animations while offering
 broad browser and viewer support.
 </p>
 <h3>How to Convert WebP to PNG:</h3> <ol> <li><strong>Upload Your WebP File:</strong> Drag and drop your WebP images into the bulk converter area to convert in browser, or switch to server-side mode for single-file server conversion.</li> <li><strong>Convert:</strong> Download your converted PNG files individually or as a ZIP archive.</li> </ol>
 <h3>Why Convert WebP to PNG?</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Lossless quality:</strong> PNG preserves every pixel: no compression artifacts, unlike JPG.</li> <li><strong>Transparency support:</strong> PNG supports alpha transparency, so transparent areas are preserved perfectly.</li> <li><strong>Universal compatibility:</strong> PNG works in all image editors, browsers, and operating systems.</li> <li><strong>Print-ready:</strong> PNG images are suitable for high-quality printing and graphic design workflows.</li> <li><strong>Editing workflow:</strong> PNG is the preferred format for image editing as it doesn't degrade with repeated saves.</li> </ul>
 <p> By default, this tool lets you batch convert multiple WebP images at once directly in your browser.
 If you need a smaller file size instead of lossless quality, try <a href="/webp-to-jpg">WebP to JPG</a>.
 Convert in the opposite direction with <a href="/png-to-webp">PNG to WebP</a>.
 </p>
 <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
 <h4>What is the difference between WebP and PNG?</h4> <p> WebP is a modern format offering both lossy and lossless compression with smaller file sizes. PNG is a
 lossless raster format with universal support. WebP files are typically smaller, but PNG is compatible
 with virtually every application and editing tool.
 </p>
 <h4>Does this tool preserve transparency?</h4> <p> Yes. Both WebP and PNG support alpha transparency, so transparent areas in your WebP image will be
 preserved exactly in the converted PNG file.
 </p>
 <h4>Is the conversion free?</h4> <p> Yes, this tool is 100% free with no watermarks, no signup, and no conversion limits.
 </p>
 <h4>What happens with animated WebP files?</h4> <p> Animated WebP files are automatically converted to APNG (Animated PNG) format right in your browser. All frames, animation timings, and transparency are preserved, and APNG is supported by all modern web browsers.
 </p>
